---
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
---

<Layout title="A Year of Mornings - Sajal Choudhary" currentPage="/books/">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <!-- Book Header -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <div class="flex flex-col md:flex-row md:items-start gap-8 mb-8">
        <!-- Book Cover -->
        <div class="flex-shrink-0">
          <img 
            src="/books/01-ayom.jpg" 
            alt="A Year of Mornings - Book Cover"
            class="w-48 h-auto rounded-lg shadow-lg border border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-600"
          />
        </div>

        <!-- Book Details -->
        <div class="flex-1">
          <div class="mb-6">
            <ul class="text-sm text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark space-y-1">
              <li><strong>Publication:</strong> February 15, 2025</li>
              <li><strong>Format:</strong> E-book & Print</li>
              <li><strong>Genre:</strong> Poetry</li>
              <li><strong>Audience:</strong> Young Adults</li>
            </ul>
          </div>

          <!-- Purchase Links -->
          <div class="space-y-3">
            <a 
              href="https://www.amazon.com/year-mornings-poems-young-adults-ebook/dp/B0DTFRPLY5?ref_=ast_author_dp"
              target="_blank"
              class="inline-block px-6 py-3 bg-accent text-white rounded-md hover:bg-opacity-90 transition-all font-medium">
              Available on Amazon
            </a>
            <p class="text-sm text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark">
              Also available through your local library's digital collection
            </p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Title Section -->
      <div class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700 pb-8">
        <h1 class="text-4xl font-bold mb-2">A Year of Mornings</h1>
        <h2 class="text-xl text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark mb-4">Poems for Young Adults</h2>
        <p class="text-lg">Sajal Choudhary</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Navigation Tabs -->
    <div class="mb-8">
      <nav class="border-b border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
        <ul class="flex space-x-8 text-sm">
          <li><a href="#about" class="py-2 border-b-2 border-accent text-accent font-medium">About the Book</a></li>
          <li><a href="#excerpts" class="py-2 text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark hover:text-accent">Sample Poems</a></li>
          <li><a href="#reviews" class="py-2 text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark hover:text-accent">Reviews</a></li>
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </div>

    <!-- About the Book Section -->
    <section id="about" class="mb-12">
      <div class="prose dark:prose-invert max-w-none">
        <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">About the Book</h3>
        
        <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <strong>A collection of poems that captures the quiet revelations found in everyday moments, 
          written for young adults navigating the complexities of growing up in an interconnected world.</strong>
        </p>

        <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
          In <em>A Year of Mornings</em>, each poem serves as a small window into the universal experiences 
          of youth: the weight of expectations, the beauty of small discoveries, the ache of change, 
          and the hope that emerges with each new day. Written from the perspective of an immigrant 
          author who has found home in multiple places, these poems speak to anyone who has ever 
          felt caught between worlds—whether those are geographical, cultural, or simply the space 
          between who you were and who you're becoming.
        </p>

        <p class="leading-relaxed mb-4">
          The collection moves through themes of identity, belonging, family, friendship, and the 
          quiet moments of self-discovery that happen in the early hours of the day. From the 
          frost-covered windows of a Finnish winter to memories of childhood in India, from the 
          anxiety of social media to the comfort of morning tea, these poems find the profound 
          in the mundane.
        </p>

        <p class="leading-relaxed mb-6">
          <em>A Year of Mornings</em> is both a love letter to the liminal spaces of young adulthood 
          and a gentle reminder that growth often happens in the quietest moments, when we're 
          barely paying attention.
        </p>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6 italic text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark">
          "These poems capture the texture of modern young adulthood with remarkable sensitivity 
          and insight. Choudhary has created something both intimate and universal."
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Sample Poems Section -->
    <section id="excerpts" class="mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">Sample Poems</h3>
      
      <div class="space-y-8">
        <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-bold mb-4">6:47 AM</h4>
          <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line">The world outside is still sleeping,
but I am here with my thoughts
and the steam rising from my cup.

This is the hour before
the notifications begin,
before the day demands
its accounting of productivity.

In this pocket of silence,
I remember who I am
without the performance.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-bold mb-4">Distance</h4>
          <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line">My mother's voice travels
7,000 kilometers in three seconds,
asking if I'm eating enough vegetables.

The lag between question and answer
contains multitudes:
visa applications, winter coats,
the taste of home cooked food,
and the weight of choices
that led me here.</div>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-6 rounded-lg">
          <h4 class="font-bold mb-4">Integration</h4>
          <div class="font-mono text-sm leading-relaxed whitespace-pre-line">They ask where I'm "really" from
and I want to say:
from the space between languages,
from the intersection of cultures,
from the morning light that looks
the same in every country
but feels different
on different skin.</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Reviews Section -->
    <section id="reviews" class="mb-12">
      <h3 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">What Readers Are Saying</h3>
      
      <div class="space-y-6">
        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
          <p class="italic mb-2">
            "These poems speak directly to the experience of being young in today's world. 
            Choudhary captures the beauty and difficulty of finding yourself with remarkable honesty."
          </p>
          <cite class="text-sm text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark">— Early Reader</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
          <p class="italic mb-2">
            "A Year of Mornings feels like having a conversation with a wise friend who 
            understands the complexity of modern young adulthood. Beautifully written and deeply moving."
          </p>
          <cite class="text-sm text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark">— Poetry Reader</cite>
        </blockquote>

        <blockquote class="border-l-4 border-accent pl-6">
          <p class="italic mb-2">
            "The immigrant experience is captured with such nuance and grace. These poems 
            will resonate with anyone who has ever felt between worlds."
          </p>
          <cite class="text-sm text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark">— Book Reviewer</cite>
        </blockquote>
      </div>
    </section>

    <!-- Call to Action -->
    <div class="bg-gray-50 dark:bg-gray-900 p-8 rounded-lg text-center">
      <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-4">Get Your Copy</h3>
      <p class="text-textSecondary dark:text-textSecondaryDark mb-6">
        <em>A Year of Mornings</em> is available as an e-book and through digital library services.
      </p>
      <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
        <a 
          href="https://www.amazon.com/year-mornings-poems-young-adults-ebook/dp/B0DTFRPLY5?ref_=ast_author_dp"
          target="_blank"
          class="px-8 py-3 bg-accent text-white rounded-md hover:bg-opacity-90 transition-all font-medium">
          Buy on Amazon
        </a>
        <a 
          href="/contact/"
          class="px-8 py-3 border border-accent text-accent rounded-md hover:bg-accent hover:bg-opacity-10 transition-all font-medium">
          Questions? Get in Touch
        </a>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- Back to Books -->
    <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-gray-200 dark:border-gray-700">
      <a href="/books/" class="text-accent hover:underline">← Back to Books</a>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>

<script>
  // Smooth scrolling for navigation tabs
  document.querySelectorAll('a[href^="#"]').forEach(anchor => {
    anchor.addEventListener('click', function (e) {
      e.preventDefault();
      const target = document.querySelector(this.getAttribute('href'));
      if (target) {
        target.scrollIntoView({
          behavior: 'smooth',
          block: 'start'
        });
      }
    });
  });
</script> 